## Scope

This license covers only the original title-project tooling and documentation
in this repository: `dusk-recomp/tools/`, `dusk-recomp/game.toml`,
`dusk-recomp/config/`, `docs/`, the root `README.md` and
`README.zh-CN.md`, and the CI configuration.

It does not cover the game. No ROM, BIOS dump, firmware image, save file or
generated recompiled game code is distributed with this repository, and none
may be redistributed as part of it. You must supply your own dump of
*Digimon World: Dusk (USA)*. *Digimon Story* and its assets are
the property of their respective rights holders; this project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by them.

It does not cover the vendored framework either. `framework/ndsrecomp`
(ndsrecomp 0.6.10) is copyright (c) 2026 Matthew Stanley and is licensed under
the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0, with portions under the MIT License
and melonDS-derived files under GPL-3.0-or-later; see
`framework/ndsrecomp/LICENSE`, `LICENSE-MIT`, `LICENSE-GPL` and
`THIRD_PARTY_ATTRIBUTION.md`. `framework/recomp-ui` is MIT, copyright (c) 2026
Matthew Stanley. FreeBIOS, used for the FreeBIOS banks, is BSD-2-Clause. Other
vendored components keep their own terms; see
[THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Nothing here grants rights to
those components beyond what their own terms allow.

Note that a built `nds_runner.exe` is a GPL-3.0-or-later combined work, because
it links the vendored melonDS GPU code through the framework. Distributing that
binary is subject to GPL-3.0-or-later, not to the MIT license above.

The port uses FreeBIOS and a generated firmware image, so a BIOS dump is not
required to build or play. A retail BIOS may optionally be supplied for
low-level development boots.
